<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela's PDVSA sees $4.4 bln net profit in 1996.</title>
<headline>Venezuela's PDVSA sees $4.4 bln net profit in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela's state oil company Petroleos de Venezuela SA (PDVSA) expects its net profits to rise to $4.4 billion in 1996, from $3.103 billion in 1995, company sources told Reuters Tuesday.</p>
<p>PDVSA President Luis Giusti estimated in July that PDVSA would make a net profit of $4 billion this year.</p>
<p>But higher-than-expected oil prices combined with sustained high levels of production will see PDVSA's profits surpass earlier estimates, said the sources, who asked not to be named.</p>
<p>-- Omar Lugo, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600</p>
